+## 2026-10-24 near-only ambiguity repair
+
+A source-pinned seed-7 lesson exposed a plausible shortcut: all three visible
+demonstrations had source cells at guide distance at most two, while the query
+required mirroring a distance-three source. The executable shortcut matched all
+demonstrations and disagreed on three query cells.
+
+Version 2.0.2 repairs that teaching hole constructively. Normal generation now
+leaves at least three columns to the right of the guide and always plants
+in-bounds sources at guide distances one and three; `self_check` enforces the
+same contract. Regression tests reproduce the original lesson and stress easy,
+medium and hard generation. The repair check covered 1,152 generated samples,
+rejected the shortcut on every sample, and matched 12 labels against protected
+Racket. This finite check does not claim uniqueness against arbitrary rules.
